{:edb/db-before-t 1860 :edb/db-after-t 1861 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535173 50 #inst "2026-10-08T18:41:16.554Z" 13194139535173 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335465 13194139535173 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335472 13194139535173 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335475 13194139535173 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186335479 13194139535173 true] [17592186335465 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335466 13194139535173 true] [17592186335465 1089 "q-14310" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335465 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535173 true] [17592186335465 1100 "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}+1$ given that  $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1.$" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335465 1113 #uuid "ef4e4fc3-8477-5354-a829-8e34e5c5f42e" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335465 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(y) & =x+C \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+C).\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1$ to find $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+C) \\\\ \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+C \\\\ \\frac{\\pi }{4} & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ C & =-\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{2}+1$ that satisfies the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\n$$" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335467 13194139535173 true] [17592186335466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335468 13194139535173 true] [17592186335466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335469 13194139535173 true] [17592186335466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335470 13194139535173 true] [17592186335466 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335471 13194139535173 true] [17592186335466 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535173 true] [17592186335466 1041 "selection" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335466 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335471 13194139535173 true] [17592186335466 1110 #uuid "db7f66ee-621c-5010-bfcb-e5d681c9977f" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335467 1034 "y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335467 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535173 true] [17592186335467 1111 #uuid "a5595c32-d167-5a2c-9469-972e442fece1" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335468 1034 "y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335468 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535173 true] [17592186335468 1111 #uuid "5b60de0c-c7aa-599a-8749-99ff0d614957" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335469 1034 "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{4})" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335469 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535173 true] [17592186335469 1111 #uuid "34bd2de0-93c2-5efd-a1fc-6f4f8b5a2dee" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335470 1034 "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{2})" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335470 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535173 true] [17592186335470 1111 #uuid "63c160d0-8bc1-5f1d-8441-c1e9e370bed3" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335471 1034 "y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335471 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535173 true] [17592186335471 1111 #uuid "54d14098-faa6-5881-afca-5a6442c450e9" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335472 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335473 13194139535173 true] [17592186335472 1089 "q-355544" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335472 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535173 true] [17592186335472 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${sec}^{2}⁡(4y){y}^{′}={sec}^{2}⁡(7x)$ that satisfies $y(0)=0.$ Assume that $-\\frac{\\pi }{8}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{8}.$\n\n$\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4y)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335472 1113 #uuid "1adf5c18-652c-5a35-ba00-6bf5024e9f68" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335472 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sec}^{2}⁡(4y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={sec}^{2}⁡(7x) \\\\ {sec}^{2}⁡(4y)\\,\\text{d}y & ={sec}^{2}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {sec}^{2}⁡(4y)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {sec}^{2}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4y) & =\\frac{1}{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(4y) & =\\frac{4}{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=4{C}_{1}.$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡(4\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{4}{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7\\cdot 0)+C \\\\ 0 & =0+C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(4y) & =\\frac{4}{7}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335473 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335474 13194139535173 true] [17592186335473 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535173 true] [17592186335473 1041 "field-1" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335473 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335474 13194139535173 true] [17592186335473 1110 #uuid "f08ee092-354d-5b2e-a653-c757d24ab056" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335474 1034 "\\frac{4}{7}\\tan(7x)" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335474 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535173 true] [17592186335474 1111 #uuid "2f9fdbbe-6c91-576e-964d-2dfe7094a9b6" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335475 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335476 13194139535173 true] [17592186335475 1089 "q-355546" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335475 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535173 true] [17592186335475 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{x}^{3}=5$ that satisfies $y(1)=6.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335475 1113 #uuid "26f23820-0414-5dbe-a547-4bdb9a3bb271" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335475 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-8{x}^{3} & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5+8{x}^{3} \\\\ \\text{d}y & =(5{x}^{-2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\text{d}y & =\\int (5{x}^{-2}+8x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =-5{x}^{-1}+4{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=6$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =6 \\\\ -5(1)^{-1}+4(1)^{2}+C & =6 \\\\ C-1 & =6 \\\\ C & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =-5{x}^{-1}+4{x}^{2}+7 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{x}+4{x}^{2}+7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335476 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335477 13194139535173 true] [17592186335476 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335478 13194139535173 true] [17592186335476 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535173 true] [17592186335476 1041 "field-1" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335476 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335477 13194139535173 true] [17592186335476 1110 #uuid "f30ee74b-194b-5ef8-a522-c1f51f015f52" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335477 1034 "4x^2-\\frac{5}{x}+7" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335477 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535173 true] [17592186335477 1111 #uuid "e83f0dba-a96b-5eef-892c-e7bd97ee16f8" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335478 1034 "4x^2-\\frac{5}{x}" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335478 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535173 true] [17592186335478 1111 #uuid "63609b85-c6f5-5030-9499-a29f4e473a1f" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335479 1017 #edb/ref 17592186335480 13194139535173 true] [17592186335479 1089 "q-4016" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335479 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535173 true] [17592186335479 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x-2y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=0.$" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335479 1113 #uuid "20669a20-777a-5d15-ade0-e739edb8a182" 13194139535173 true] [17592186335479 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x-2y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{-2y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{e}^{2y}} \\\\ {e}^{2y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{2y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{2y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2y} & ={e}^{x}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {e}^{2y} & =2{e}^{x}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2{C}_{1}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{0}+C) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+C) & =0 \\\\ 2+C & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x-2y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=0$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2{e}^{x}-1).\n$$" 13194139535173 true] 